      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Houseplant gardenia (RHS: short-lived, tricky) and a hardy garden shrub (NC State: zones 7b to 11b, 4 to 8 ft) in one row. Needs ericaceous compost and soft water. Care values come from the RHS growing guide (indoor, full page); NC State was truncated (about 39 of 51 thousand characters verbatim, the attribute table via summary), so its growth rate, habit and light-by-hours are weaker. Light: RHS warm and bright out of direct sun; NC State bright indirect or partial shade. Temperature: RHS day 21 to 24 C, winter 10 to 15 C, nights under 18 C for flowering. Humidity: RHS high and uniform, no figure. Size left unknown: NC State's shrub size is the outdoor one and the RHS guide gives none. Toxicity: ASPCA toxic to dogs and cats (genioposide, gardenoside; mild vomiting and diarrhoea, hives); NC State low severity for humans with the same mild signs. Graded 1 by the agent; hives not in our symptom list."
      },
